    "perplexity": {
      "description": "Roll With You is Eli “Paperboy” Reed & The True Loves’ breakthrough 2008 album, a brash and affectionate revival of classic 1960s soul, Southern funk, and Chicago blues. Reed’s raw, full-throated vocals lead a tight, groove-focused band through punchy originals such as “Stake Your Claim,” “The Satisfier,” “Take My Love With You,” and “The Boom Boom,” balancing gritty urgency with the warmth of vintage rhythm and blues. The songs were written or co-written by Reed, giving the retro sound a personal, contemporary energy rather than treating it as mere imitation.\n\nOriginally released in 2008, the album helped establish Reed as an important figure in the modern soul revival and earned him a national and international following. Its direct songwriting, brassy arrangements, and live-band intensity make it especially effective as a complete listen, capturing the excitement of a young performer steeped in soul history but determined to push the style forward. Yep Roc later issued a 23-track deluxe remastered edition in 2018, expanding the original 11-song album with additional material while preserving the record’s central impact.",
